{"content":[{"c":["HOUSE OF GOD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Common phrase used in the ancient Near Eastern world for a structure used to accommodate a deity or his servants. In the OT it referred to the tabernacle (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.23.18","r":"Deut.23.18","rawR":"Deut.23.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.23.18","value":"Deut.23.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 23:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.31-32","r":"1Chr.6.31-32","rawR":"1Chr.6.31-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.31-32","value":"1Chr.6.31-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:31-32"},"), Solomon’s temple (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.8.11-20","r":"1Kgs.8.11-20","rawR":"1Kgs.8.11-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.8.11-20","value":"1Kgs.8.11-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 8:11-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.12.27","r":"1Kgs.12.27","rawR":"1Kgs.12.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.12.27","value":"1Kgs.12.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.20.1","r":"Jer.20.1","rawR":"Jer.20.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.20.1","value":"Jer.20.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 20:1"},"), national shrines, or pagan temples (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.9.4","r":"Judg.9.4","rawR":"Judg.9.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.9.4","value":"Judg.9.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 9:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.10.21","r":"2Kgs.10.21","rawR":"2Kgs.10.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.10.21","value":"2Kgs.10.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 10:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In NT times the OT custom of referring to the temple as the “house of God” was still employed (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.12.4","r":"Matt.12.4","rawR":"Matt.12.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.12.4","value":"Matt.12.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 12:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.2.26","r":"Mark.2.26","rawR":"Mark.2.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.2.26","value":"Mark.2.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 2:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.11.17","r":"Mark.11.17","rawR":"Mark.11.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.11.17","value":"Mark.11.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.6.4","r":"Luke.6.4","rawR":"Luke.6.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.6.4","value":"Luke.6.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 6:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.2.16-17","r":"John.2.16-17","rawR":"John.2.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.2.16-17","value":"John.2.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 2:16-17"},"), but with some significant changes. After Christ’s ascension, the church viewed itself as the house of God (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.3.9","r":"1Cor.3.9","rawR":"1Cor.3.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.3.9","value":"1Cor.3.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 3:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.3.6","r":"Heb.3.6","rawR":"Heb.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.3.6","value":"Heb.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 3:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.2.5","r":"1Pet.2.5","rawR":"1Pet.2.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.2.5","value":"1Pet.2.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pt 2:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.4.17","r":"1Pet.4.17","rawR":"1Pet.4.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.4.17","value":"1Pet.4.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:17"},"). God no longer dwelt in buildings made by human hands but in the lives of those who confess Jesus as Lord."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Tabernacle_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Tabernacle_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Tabernacle_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Tabernacle"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Temple_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Temple_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Temple_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Temple"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HouseofGod","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 23:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.23.18","rawQueryValue":"Deut.23.18","sourceRefExact":"Deut.23.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:31-32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?